{"availability":"available","full":"Abdalla-Eldoumani/tajweed-trainer","name":"tajweed-trainer","description":"Interactive tajweed trainer: color-coded Quran text, guided lessons, quizzes, and audio from renowned reciters. Client-only Next.js PWA.","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":4,"forks":1,"created":"2026-02-20T11:29:01Z","updated":"2026-10-11T00:26:48Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://tajweedtrainer.vercel.app","topics":["arabic","education","islam","mushaf","nextjs","pwa","quran","react","recitation","tailwindcss","tajweed","typescript"],"demo":"https://tajweedtrainer.vercel.app/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T14:52:53.394Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T14:52:53.394Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T14:52:53.394Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T14:52:53.394Z","stars":4,"forks":1}],"technologies":["React","Next.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A bilingual (English / Arabic) web app for learning Tajweed, the rules of proper Quran recitation. It pairs nine color-coded lesson modules and practice quizzes with a full 604-page Madinan Mushaf reader, where tapping a verse opens a focused overlay for playback, memorization, notes, and meaning, and a follow-along highlights each word as it is recited. It ships in five art-directed manuscript themes and runs entirely in the browser: no account, no server, and offline as an installed app, with progress kept in localStorage.","The text, the color coding, and the per-verse recitation follow Hafs 'an 'Asim, the most widely used Qira'ah. Quranic text and audio come from established APIs; the rule explanations and examples come from JSON that is reviewed against primary sources before it is marked verified."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Abdalla-Eldoumani/tajweed-trainer/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"84cebbec8d716b44e605b271e96c14dce3d6c27a937870150e1d841260b86c99","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T14:52:53.558Z"},"overv